__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
dist/
build/
# mkdocs build output (`poetry run mkdocs build`)
site/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
# Build reports -- one is written per `connkg build` run, so routine rebuilds
# would otherwise pile up in the diff. They are good provenance (host, versions,
# input digests, stage timings, peak memory), so keep the ones worth keeping
# deliberately:  git add -f reports/build_<date>.md
reports/build_*.md
# the same for `connkg skeletons`, which writes one per pass
reports/skeletons_*.md
# real connectome downloads (FlyWire is CC BY-NC-SA; keep it out of the repo)
data/
fafb_v783/
# source papers, for the DocKG corpus beside the graph. Open access, but the
# publishers' PDFs are theirs to distribute, not ours -- and they are ~45 MB.
# The text extracted from them is derived and stays out too; what IS tracked
# is the manifest saying which papers the corpus was built from.
papers/*.pdf
papers/text/
.DS_Store
uv.lock

# === Rendered output (renders/), following quiltwright's layout -- see
# renders/README.md and docs/rendering.md.
# stills/ and views/ are local scratch (a working --preview PNG, per-view
# captures); quilts/ holds Looking Glass quilts (tens of MB each); reports/
# is reserved for future per-render provenance records and stays tracked --
# the only account of how a gitignored quilt was made.
renders/*
!renders/README.md
!renders/reports/
# Quilts are never committed regardless of where they land -- these two
# patterns have no slash, so git applies them at every depth, matching
# quiltwright's own .gitignore.
*_qs[0-9]*x[0-9]*a*.png
*_qs[0-9]*x[0-9]*a*.mp4
# === end rendered output ===

# === KG generated artifacts (normalized across the fleet) ===
# Databases, vector indexes and model caches are transient and
# reproducible. snapshots/ is TRACKED and must never be ignored --
# never use a bare `**/.<ns>/` pattern here, it swallows snapshots too.

**/.pycodekg/*.sqlite
**/.pycodekg/*.sqlite-shm
**/.pycodekg/*.sqlite-wal
**/.pycodekg/*.db
**/.pycodekg/models

**/.dockg/*.sqlite
**/.dockg/*.sqlite-shm
**/.dockg/*.sqlite-wal
**/.dockg/*.db
**/.dockg/models
**/.dockg/embeddings.json

**/.connectomekg/*.sqlite
**/.connectomekg/*.sqlite-shm
**/.connectomekg/*.sqlite-wal
**/.connectomekg/*.db
**/.connectomekg/models
# neuropil mesh cache (connkg meshes) and synapse-graph cache -- derived
**/.connectomekg/*.npz
# simplified skeleton cache (connkg skeletons) -- derived from FlyWire data.
# The cache is a DIRECTORY of part-NNNN.parquet shards, so the shards sit one
# level deeper than every other pattern here and need their own rule.
**/.connectomekg/*.parquet
**/.connectomekg/skeletons/
# the partial a cache is built in before it is moved into place; an
# interrupted run removes its own, but a killed process cannot
**/.connectomekg/*.part

# Agent scratch dirs (Claude Code / Codex)
.agents/
.codex/

# MCP server config -- machine-specific, contains absolute paths
.mcp.json.sav
# === end KG generated artifacts ===
